{"event":{"data":{"artifact_rev":null,"commit_sha":null,"decisions":["Add a minimal HTTP hello endpoint using only the Python 3 standard library (http.server). Create hello.py at the repo root defining a request handler (and a way to run a server) where GET /hello responds with HTTP 200, Content-Type text/plain, and a body of exactly 'hello'. Add test_hello.py at the repo root with one unittest that starts the server (e.g. on an ephemeral port in a background thread), issues GET /hello, and asserts the status, content type, and body. No other files are added or changed; there is no prior stage to wait for (the repo currently has no app code)."],"doubts":[],"run_id":"r-41-3","state":"triage"},"epoch":1,"kind":"handoff_accepted","prev":"74e49ac728c0537a388ad664e125533bf04d2de85b713a2fb4a2d46913976d90","schema":1,"seq":13},"line":"event","schema":1,"seq":13}
